q.if .tfstate deleted then it will restore it from backup using remote backend but suppose backup file also got deletd then from it it maintained the state again.
sol.If the Terraform state file and its backup are deleted but S3 versioning is enabled, the state can be restored from previous object versions. 
    If versioning is not enabled and all copies are lost, Terraform cannot automatically reconstruct the state. The infrastructure may still exist in the cloud 
    provider, but the state must be rebuilt by importing existing resources using terraform import. That's why remote backends, versioning, and backup strategies are
    critical for secure state management.
    S3 State Bucket - enable Versioning , Cross Region Replication, Backup Account
